Forrest Gump was a big-time  crowd-pleaser and a sequel would have  definitely also earned stacks of cash at  the box office  so what kept a potential part 2 from  ever hitting theaters well stop eating a  shrimp and grab your running shoes as we  find out why Forrest Gump - never got  made  Once Upon a Time Tom Hanks was best  known as a comedian but then the  oscar-winning double whammy of  Philadelphia and Forrest Gump turned him  into an esteemed actor and gave him  serious Hollywood clout following those  back-to-back lead actor wins Hank's  could have easily made a Gump sequel but  instead he opted for Apollo 13 so why  didn't he revisit his iconic character  in 1995 Hanks said that he didn't think  Forrest Gump - was a good idea for one  thing is he told Entertainment Weekly he  was tired of all those catchphrases but  more importantly he was worried a sequel  would hurt the legacy of the original  film as he put it I have to confess I  don't see this as a franchise a sequel  would ruin what we had done it would be  like jaws - while Forrest Scott might  seem like a distinctly cinematic  experience the movie was actually based  on a novel by Winston groom so when it  came time to adapt the story for the big  screen  paramount tapped Eric Roth to write the  screenplay Ross is an incredibly  respected writer who won an Academy  Award for his Gump script and went on to  nab even more Oscar nominations for the  likes of The Curious Case of Benjamin  Button and a star is born and as it  turns out in between writing all these  acclaimed screenplays Roth was busy  hammering out a script for a Forrest  Gump sequel for a brief moment it looked  like we might return to the world of  Lieutenant Dan and the Bubba Gump shrimp  company but while Roth is a fantastic  writer who's produced some spectacular  movies his Forrest Gump - script might  not be his most mainstream work Forrest  Gump is a movie that wants you to cry  and the saddest scene in the entire film  is probably when Jenny dies leaving  Forrest absolutely wrecked played by  Robin Wright jenny has lived a pretty  rough life and she eventually contracts  a mysterious virus that doctors can't  cure it is implied that she succumbed to  AIDS and that was going to play a big  role in the aborted sequel according to  Eric Roth Gump and his son now lived in  Florida and everyone in his community  was going to freak out when they learned  Forrest  Jr  contracted AIDS from his mom as Roth  noted to consequence of sound we had a  funny sequence where they were  desegregating busing in Florida at the  same time so people were angry about  either the busing for their kids having  to go to school with the kid who had  AIDS so there was a big conflict so  according to Roth Forrest Gump who was  going to use racism and the AIDS crisis  together for the sake of a comedy bit  those are two highly sensitive topics  that most movie goers would probably  agree aren't the best fodder for humor  in addition to the phenomenal acting and  nostalgic soundtrack Forrest Gump is  also praised for its visual effects the  folks at Industrial Light and Magic  actually won an Oscar for their  incredible work perhaps the most  impressive accomplishment was putting  Tom Hanks into archival footage  alongside famous historical figures like  Richard Nixon and John F Kennedy Eric  Roth planned on having Forrest encounter  even more famous figures in the sequel  including an iconic cameo that doesn't  sound like a great fit evidently Forrest  was going to be very involved in the  saga of OJ Simpson somehow he would be  the one responsible for tossing the  bloody glove found at Simpsons Brentwood  home stranger still Forrest would  somehow wind up in the back of Simpson's  white Bronco as the football star leads  the police on the slowest car chase in  history the OJ Simpson trial was  obviously a huge news story in the 90s  but it would probably feel bizarrely out  of place in a Forrest Gump sequel for  all its happy moments Forrest Gump is  ultimately a tragedy after all it ends  just moments after Forrest gives a  tearful goodbye at Jenny's grave as for  the sequel Eric Roth had no intention of  giving our chocolate loving hero a happy  ending speaking with Yahoo Roth  explained that Forrest would have a new  love interest a Native American woman he  meets while riding a bus she was going  to be a nursery school teacher and every  day Forrest would sit on a park bench  and share a lunch break with her but she  wouldn't be teaching at any old nursery  school instead it would be located  inside the Federal Building in Oklahoma  City where in 1995 Timothy McVeigh set  off a truck full of explosives Forrest  girlfriend was going to die in the blast  worse still it would happen while  Forrest was sitting on that bench as the  building explodes right behind him which  sounds more than a little  so if Eric Roth had a script ready to go  how come Forrest Gump tune never got  made it turns out that he turned in his  final draft on September 10th 2001 the  very next day the world was turned  upside down the 9/11 terrorist attacks  impacted the production of quite a few  films and it stopped the Gump sequel  from even getting past the screenplay  face after all the movie was supposed to  end with Forrest girlfriend dying in one  of the most devastating terrorist  attacks in American history and that  just wasn't going to fly in the  aftermath of 9/11 so on the day of the  attacks he met up with Tom Hanks and  director Robert Zemeckis to commiserate  we looked at each other and said this  movie has no meaning anymore in that  sense so it's probably for the best that  Forrest Gump who never happened from  what we know of the screenplay  it doesn't sound like it would have been  anywhere near as beloved as the original  check out one of our newest videos right  here plus even more looper videos about  your favorite stuff for coming soon  subscribe to our YouTube channel and hit  the bell so you don't miss a single one  [Music]  you  [Music]
 

